#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by Multiple Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be6986a1-d2a7-5720-8d02-8ba1f861273a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be6986a1-d2a7-5720-8d02-8ba1f861273a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283613} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebba82c0-7f08-53d4-a72b-d1667ec8a676" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283612} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d42bd5-10cf-5458-8763-29efc0a2fa60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d42bd5-10cf-5458-8763-29efc0a2fa60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283615} :answer-field/id #uuid "fde68ac4-d4eb-57de-8e20-e49f91528eb2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8583426-4bc3-5bad-8b87-9fd0547dfc61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8583426-4bc3-5bad-8b87-9fd0547dfc61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283617} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b787382-aa99-50fd-8114-e64cabffdd97" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283616} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8464f5c8-8303-57b1-9cbc-d044d9175cd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8464f5c8-8303-57b1-9cbc-d044d9175cd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283619} :answer-field/id #uuid "80a94fa4-fad8-530b-baa7-fdedb438a6b8" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "362f84f6-da26-53e5-b785-e716fe57b192" :question/math-academy-id "q-274701" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{90}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={30}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={120}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={210}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={300}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={30}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={120}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}={210}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}={300}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent Function Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48023e4b-c5e8-59e9-9dfb-6d957ec5e024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283622} {:answer/id #uuid "eb320fbd-d953-539a-9821-9e6d26e2001b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283623} {:answer/id #uuid "ee846222-021c-5367-8296-b665ce9afeb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283624} {:answer/id #uuid "0258d2dd-dda4-538a-a8f7-1450b914d022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283625} {:answer/id #uuid "da2fe10a-31ba-5123-8e80-121216668f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb320fbd-d953-539a-9821-9e6d26e2001b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283623} :answer-field/id #uuid "64f888a9-fca8-58ba-be12-21695875f0dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c23519c0-b4cf-5df9-bbf3-a99ec81e76c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-65851" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=1$ for $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{(4n+1)\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}=-\\pi .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Tangent Function Transformed by Multiple Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f7a6ff-eca7-5e4f-bbf2-11db9814c688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283629} {:answer/id #uuid "85d5cded-a291-585e-a193-c7978bc54283" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283630} {:answer/id #uuid "b8edc3e9-ed09-5ca3-95f2-602ede5de8f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283631} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8fe5ce-852a-5e08-b928-f2f61f9165c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283632} {:answer/id #uuid "88326791-532a-5f2c-935c-5fdc42d8e1ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e8fe5ce-852a-5e08-b928-f2f61f9165c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283632} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c0ddc64-d13d-57c7-b589-9db856cfb9c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "13830fee-20a1-5f06-9a68-65b5fe7b7a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-8476" :question/problem "Consider the equation $3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Given that the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(3n+1)\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{6},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{2}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and ${x}_{3}=\\frac{7\\pi }{6},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{6}=\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent Function Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4744d360-e084-557e-9788-b79051b0a470" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283636} {:answer/id #uuid "2447218f-56c9-573b-8e6a-a78d17c8c2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283637} {:answer/id #uuid "a3875b88-aa63-50a2-9a80-405381d560c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283638} {:answer/id #uuid "96ff6c95-be57-5b92-85b0-41000b051c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283639} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9e429a-c7ff-5b61-9512-4016137f2fd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4744d360-e084-557e-9788-b79051b0a470" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283636} :answer-field/id #uuid "72684fcf-8a1d-562b-a067-4c43bb6e8957" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "527f7f27-5579-5862-bf98-9b454d638e7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-8477" :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=1$ for $0\\le x<\\pi .$ If the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent Function Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3689f59-a2f5-536c-a227-47176b889a9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi }{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283643} {:answer/id #uuid "8993e47e-f568-547a-ab5b-823258203bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283644} {:answer/id #uuid "926b7e8a-c99b-5e5d-b545-4cc5f7c706d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283645} {:answer/id #uuid "d10aa117-11a5-58e1-8b2d-88f7a026d12b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283646} {:answer/id #uuid "ed0ad446-60b7-5d7f-89f5-e513e559b68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi }{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "926b7e8a-c99b-5e5d-b545-4cc5f7c706d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283645} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d7164eb-5953-58f0-bc2e-73f0a8967b7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d166a54d-b12b-5548-b477-26b9a92e7cfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-8559" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})+\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $0\\le x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})+\\sqrt{3}=0 \\\\  & \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})=-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{24}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(12n+25)\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24},\\frac{13\\pi }{24}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{13\\pi }{24}=\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$"}]}
